# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/ship-4 window (the combined ship candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/ship-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TC5 (TIMED, the ABAB's D): the CANDIDATE of the concurrent tier plan (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent-timed, scenario tier_concurrent_timed: no row digests, no
# extent audit, the tier's own audits off), profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4. The candidate is a TRAFFIC profile under an owner traffic
# waiver whose decision is PENDING: it boots in a gate or a smoke and logs the word (c2_serving_job.read_bake refuses a PENDING profile only at the BUILD). THE ABAB: TC2
# control, TC3 candidate, TC4 control, TC5 candidate, every boot a fresh reset. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI
# push, no other job beside it. READ each: the plan verdict PASS (the stall budget is JUDGED here: no seat waited longer than the Lever N decode gap floor, 8 s, between two
# tokens in any window), then the four together: python3 scripts/ci/tier_concurrent_compare.py <TC2 results> <TC3 results> <TC4 results> <TC5 results> (A control, B
# candidate, C control repeat, D candidate repeat): exit 0 needs every seat IDENTICAL over its common tokens (the seven streams unchanged by the candidate), the returning,
# long-prompt and cold-twin answers IDENTICAL across the profiles, and no longest wait over the budget; it prints the round p50/p99 of each arm window by window, the
# CANDIDATE arm's p99 against the CONTROL arm's (percent) and the control-to-control FLOOR. THE CONTROL IS THE APPROVED FUSION SHIP PROFILE, which has no tier, no octo and
# the 19,968-block pool: the returning session is re-prefilled cold beside the seven seats there. The candidate's p99 therefore mixes the tier's restore stall with the octo
# rounds' speed-up; the tier's own cost against its own control is the tier pack's (references/fusion-jobs/tier). THE LEVER-FLAVOURED READ: in the candidate arm the lines
# "host tier restore" and "host tier spill" must be in the log (else NOT_EXERCISED) and the [OCTO] round lines must show shape=octo with live 7-8 during the control window.
# Estimate: 50 minutes. TELEMETRY: the prefix step has no sidecar.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
